From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn: link UFS to the inline crypto engine

The SM8750 dtsi in 7.2 declares the ICE at crypto@1d88000 but does not
reference it from the UFS node, so ufs_qcom_ice_init() gets -EOPNOTSUPP
and ufs-qcom never suspends the engine. The ICE driver enables its core
clock at probe, and with no consumer to suspend it the clock stays
prepared across system sleep and holds GPLL4 and the XO. Add the
qcom,ice link as current mainline does.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
@@ -1413,6 +1413,14 @@
 
 &ufs_mem_hc {
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 215 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+	/*
+	 * Link the inline crypto engine so ufs-qcom owns its clocks. Without
+	 * this the ICE driver leaves gcc_ufs_phy_ice_core_clk enabled from
+	 * probe and nobody turns it off, which keeps GPLL4 and the XO voted
+	 * on through suspend. Mainline adds the same property after 7.2.
+	 */
+	qcom,ice = <&ice>;
 
 	vcc-supply = <&vreg_l17b_2p5>;
 	vcc-max-microamp = <1300000>;
